{
  "originalPrompt": "## Context & Goal\n\nIntegrate the Google Analytics toolkit into VoiceOS via Composio using OAuth2. This enables the VoiceOS agent to run analytics reports and retrieve metadata on behalf of authenticated users.\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\n- Use **Composio** as the MCP provider for all Google Analytics tool calls\n- Auth method: **OAuth2** — implement the Composio OAuth2 connection flow for Google Analytics\n- Expose only the following **approved tools** (no others):\n    - `Run report`\n    - `Run realtime report`\n    - `Get metadata`\n- UX/UI requirements:\n    - OAuth2 connect/disconnect UI for Google Analytics account linking\n    - Loading states during report queries\n    - Success/error toast notifications for failed queries\n    - Clear error messaging if OAuth token expires or is revoked\n\n## Relevant Files / Code Paths\n\n- Composio SDK integration layer\n- OAuth2 connection flow component\n- Tool execution handler\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ]  Google Analytics OAuth2 connection flow works end-to-end via Composio\n- [ ]  All 3 approved tools are callable by the VoiceOS agent\n- [ ]  No unapproved tools are exposed\n- [ ]  Loading states render correctly during report queries\n- [ ]  OAuth token refresh is handled gracefully\n\naction descriptions in the Actions panel get cut off after two lines with no way to expand. Keep them short and user-facing (agent instructions don't need to be shown there)",
